Z||000010||BAM-BAM||11-30-2000||08:11 AM||||   I talked with Mike about this extensively and heres how it went down. Mike got his carpets through ACC. When I orderd my interior which included carpet, all things were a go. Just before everything was to ship I called mike and asked how things were progressing. He told me there was a problem with the carpet, that his supplier (ACC) said they would no longer be making the carpets in the material that Mike was previously using. They (ACC) sent him a sample of what they were to provide in the future for Mikes critique. Mike was unimpressed and told them no thanks. He then discontinued his carpeting for bad buisness reasons. He told me to call ACC directly and ask if they still carried the carpet that he was previously using. They (ACC) told me that they haven't discontinued any carpet lines (they lied to MIKE). There rational as far as we (Mike and I)could tell, must have been a buisness decision. Mike was selling their carpets cheaper than they were, or should I say more reasonably priced. They (ACC) must have felt that this was cutting into their proffit margins and created a "Shortage of Convenience".  Mike is a stand up guy that offers a quality product. He evidently felt slighted and figured he would stick to what he does best and he does leather THE BEST! ACC still has the carpet that mike used and it is still available. It's a little more expensive than mike for the complete car (about $100.00 more the way I ordered it). That's all I know. I told Mike that I would keep things under my hat untill the time came, the time is now.<P>  Peace, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||12
Z||000011||William||11-30-2000||09:45 AM||||I see the headliner and firewall panel has been dropped too. Did Mike make these products or can we get them from his source?||||reg||1
Z||000012||BAM-BAM||11-30-2000||10:53 AM||||  Mike made these pieces as well. He got out of the fiberglass buisness, said it was to dirty with all the sanding and cutting. He mainly wants to stick to the leather side of things now. The headliner panels are available through the Fiero store. ACC can supply carpet to recover the firewall panel.<P> Peace, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000013||ChopTop||12-01-2000||08:59 AM||||I received a reply back from ACC asking me for my address so they could send me a sample of the carpeting.  I wasn't sure what grades they carried, I asked they send me a sample of something for a first class interior.  Guess I'll find out.  It's a shame we are forced to hodgepod our interiors together.  Because we are now forced to deal with different vendors anything other than a black interior may result in receiving different shades of a color, leading to an interior that looks mismatched color wise.  An option would be to go to a interior professional, the type street rodders use.  The thought of how much money that would cost is scary, but I would imagine you could be resonable assured both the type of materials and colors used for the various interior pieces would match.    ||||reg||1
